sha256":"9e924607d14c569e846781a83c93ff7efae819e3c3970699902b3d22eacd4438"},{"path":"src/main/java/mssql/googlecode/concurrentlinkedhashmap/EntryWeigher.java","sha256":"bc5ed63ced9d077cf9bb358c3bd766dcfde80fb87ca2b6d94205dee03f7b23a8"},{"path":"src/main/java/mssql/googlecode/concurrentlinkedhashmap/EvictionListener.java","sha256":"eee48953604b768e09c2b648210e40eca9e296ead87d9b352bcddea509e1edaa"},{"path":"src/main/java/mssql/googlecode/concurrentlinkedhashmap/Linked.java","sha256":"d63fe969af221b4af905a854010784605b571cf25ea03231efb33230f0256da4"},{"path":"src/main/java/mssql/googlecode/concurrentlinkedhashmap/LinkedDeque.java","sha256":"9ff5000a45f038ee3d48400d8b4b2988022e7b7a402d04fe96fe54ec5fa5d5b7"},{"path":"src/main/java/mssql/googlecode/concurrentlinkedhashmap/Weigher.java","sha256":"e327dac4ce8f8141640703c0ef169b752e437d73820e508fca92de45a135e4b8"},{"path":"src/main/java/mssql/googlecode/concurrentlinkedhashmap/Weighers.java","sha256":"7512d7a9f98836be472cfa7ac127153d008a592aee9736ca69e1fa86fc308903"},{"path":"src/main/java/mssql/googlecode/concurrentlinkedhashmap/package-info.java","sha256":"7f0f842ef642be0ce0ed6cd8e7cef51bb284164611a189d57852e872f706e58d"},{"path":"src/main/java/mssql/security/provider/MD4.java","sha256":"812e7b930c7a4075c15ea4abc78b9d0ab5c1997874176d481e24d94655603b5a"}],"queries":[{"id":"repoqa-567b765592e0cc131541","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To enhance an error message by appending a unique connection identifier if the connection is active and the identifier is available.\n2. **Input**: A string representing an error message and a connection object.\n3. **Output**: A string which is either the original error message or the error message appended with a unique connection identifier.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first checks if the connection object is not null and is active. If so, it retrieves the unique connection identifier. If the identifier is available, it appends this identifier to the original error message using a specific format. If the connection is not active or the identifier is not available, it returns the original error message.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/SQLServerException.java","grade":2,"spans":[[395,409]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-cceb6c28d22756f3707e","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to securely transmit a time value in an encrypted form as part of a remote procedure call (RPC) to a SQL Server, ensuring the confidentiality of the data.\n2. **Input**: The function takes a calendar object representing the time to be encrypted, nanoseconds to add precision, a scale to define the precision of the time value, a boolean indicating if the parameter is an output, and a statement object for SQL operations.\n3. **Output**: There is no direct return value; however, the function writes encrypted time data to a network stream or buffer for SQL Server communication.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - Initially, the function checks if the configuration allows sending time as datetime, throwing an exception if not permitted.\n   - It sets the parameter type for the RPC.\n   - If the calendar object is null, it writes a null value; otherwise, it encrypts the time data (including nanoseconds and scale adjustments) and writes this encrypted data.\n   - Finally, it writes metadata related to the encryption and the time type to the stream or buffer.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/IOBuffer.java","grade":2,"spans":[[5808,5824]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-98796e9597ddf52141bb","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To strip the leading and trailing single quotes from a given string if both are present.\n2. **Input**: A string that may or may not be enclosed in single quotes.\n3. **Output**: The same string but without the leading and trailing single quotes if it started and ended with them; otherwise, the original string is returned unchanged.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first checks the length of the string. It then examines if the first and last characters of the string are single quotes. If both conditions are met, it returns a new string with the first and last characters removed. If not, it returns the original string.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/SQLServerBulkBatchInsertRecord.java","grade":2,"spans":[[198,201]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-a7b16e7ca1bf51059b54","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To ensure that the holdability parameter provided matches one of the acceptable values defined by the JDBC specification and supported by the driver.\n2. **Input**: An integer representing the holdability setting for a result set.\n3. **Output**: Throws an exception if the input is not valid; otherwise, does not return any value.\n4. **Procedure**: The function checks if the input integer matches either of the two predefined valid constants. If the input does not match any of these constants, it formats an error message and throws an exception indicating that the holdability value is invalid.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/SQLServerConnection.java","grade":2,"spans":[[6864,6869]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-d15e3599fcaaccbad69c","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to inform registered listeners about specific activities or errors related to a database connection. It either signals that a connection has been closed or that an error has occurred, prompting appropriate actions like connection removal or recycling.\n2. **Input**: An exception object that indicates an error (if any); if this object is null, it implies the connection is simply being closed without errors.\n3. **Output**: There is no direct output returned by this function; however, it triggers side effects through event notifications to listeners.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - Logs the error if logging is enabled and an exception is provided.\n   - If an exception is present, it locks a mutex, closes the last proxy connection (if it exists), and releases the mutex.\n   - Regardless of whether an exception was provided, it locks another mutex and iterates through all registered event listeners to dispatch either a connection closed or an error occurred event, then unlocks the mutex.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/SQLServerPooledConnection.java","grade":2,"spans":[[171,211]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-5d53a371d464387ee953","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To retrieve a list of encryption details associated with a specific column encryption key (CEK), which includes multiple encrypted values of the CEK when using different column master keys (CMKs).\n2. **Input**: There are no direct inputs as this method does not take parameters; it operates on the internal state of its class instance.\n3. **Output**: Returns a list of objects, each containing details such as the encrypted CEK, database and key identifiers, key path, key store name, and encryption algorithm used.\n4. **Procedure**: The method directly accesses a pre-stored list within the class instance that holds the encryption details for the CEK. It simply returns this list to the caller without any modifications or additional processing.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/AE.java","grade":2,"spans":[[57,59]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-a42de57d6cc095628463","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To retrieve the password used for accessing the trust store in a database connection configuration.\n2. **Input**: None required directly by the method.\n3. **Output**: Returns a string representing the password of the trust store, or null if no password is set.\n4. **Procedure**: Accesses the connection properties to fetch the value associated with the trust store password key. If the key is not found or the value is not set, it returns null.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/SQLServerDataSource.java","grade":2,"spans":[[420,422]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-ed54ed75682ba85bf90a","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To generate a 6-byte random array that serves as a unique client identifier, mimicking a MAC address, for use in network communications. This is used to avoid personal identifiable information (PII) issues.\n2. **Input**: None.\n3. **Output**: A 6-byte array of random numbers.\n4. **Procedure**: The function creates a byte array of size 6, then fills this array with random bytes generated by an instance of the `Random` class.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/SQLServerConnection.java","grade":2,"spans":[[324,329]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-4b54b7d7efdccbbde654","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: This function is designed to compute the NTLMv2 response for authentication purposes, using a given hash key and a challenge message from a server.\n2. **Input**: A byte array representing the NT response hash key.\n3. **Output**: A byte array that represents the computed NTLMv2 response, which includes both the NT proof string and the client challenge blob.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - Generate a random client nonce.\n   - Create a client challenge blob using the client nonce.\n   - Concatenate the server challenge with the client challenge blob.\n   - Compute the NT proof string using HMAC-MD5 with the response key and the concatenated challenge.\n   - Update the session base key using HMAC-MD5 with the response key and the NT proof string.\n   - Concatenate the NT proof string with the client challenge blob to form the final response.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/NTLMAuthentication.java","grade":2,"spans":[[703,716]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-eb0eae1f8d554fdf3a6c","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to retrieve metadata about a specific parameter used in a stored procedure or a parameterized SQL statement.\n2. **Input**: It accepts an integer representing the index of the parameter for which metadata is required.\n3. **Output**: Returns a map containing metadata about the specified parameter, such as data type, column type, precision, scale, and nullability.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first checks if the SQL statement involves a table-valued parameter (TVP) and if it is structured to return a value. Depending on these conditions, it adjusts the index to access the correct metadata from a pre-stored list of metadata for each parameter. The metadata is then retrieved from this list based on the adjusted index and returned.\n","group":"microsoft/mssql-jdbc","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/main/java/com/microsoft/sqlserver/jdbc/SQLServerParameterMetaData.java","grade":2,"spans":[[389,396]]}],"answerability":"answerable"}]}
